{"id":"109a7d19bf667168837f32929e00b791e195d14d","axis":"silent","repo":"huggingface/transformers","sha":"109a7d19bf667168837f32929e00b791e195d14d","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".gitattributes","lines":["@@ -273,6 +273,10 @@ src/transformers/models/ijepa/modeling_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/informer/modeling_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/inkling/configuration_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/inkling/modeling_*.py linguist-generated=true","+src/transformers/models/inkling2/configuration_*.py linguist-generated=true","+src/transformers/models/inkling2/image_*.py linguist-generated=true","+src/transformers/models/inkling2/modeling_*.py linguist-generated=true","+src/transformers/models/inkling2/processing_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/instructblipvideo/configuration_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/instructblipvideo/modeling_*.py linguist-generated=true"," src/transformers/models/internlm3/configuration_*.py linguist-generated=true"],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/source/en/_toctree.yml","lines":["@@ -1429,6 +1429,8 @@","         title: Idefics3","       - local: model_doc/inkling","         title: Inkling","+      - local: model_doc/inkling2","+        title: Inkling2","       - local: model_doc/instructblip","         title: InstructBLIP","       - local: model_doc/instructblipvideo"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/source/en/model_doc/inkling2.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,166 @@","+<!--Copyright 2026 the HuggingFace Team. All rights reserved.","+","+Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the \"License\");","+you may not use this file except in compliance with the License.","+You may obtain a copy of the License at","+","+    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0","+","+Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software","+distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,","+WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.","+See the License for the specific language governing permissions and","+limitations under the License.","+","+","+⚠️ Note that this file is in Markdown but contains specific syntax for our doc-builder (similar to MDX) that may not be rendered properly in your Markdown viewer.","+","+-->","+*This model was contributed to Hugging Face Transformers on 2026-11-11.*","+","+# Inkling 2 Small","+","+[Inkling 2 Small](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8) is a multimodal model from [Thinking Machines Lab](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines) that accepts text and image inputs and generates text outputs. It is intended for use in English and other languages, and across multiple coding languages. It keeps the decoder of [Inkling](./inkling), with learned relative attention, short causal convolutions and mixture-of-experts layers, and adds block attention residuals, gated attention with a learned sink and dynamic key/value convolutions. The language backbone consists of 48 mixture-of-experts decoder layers, each routing tokens to 8 of 384 experts. The model has 594B total and 17B active parameters. Images are encoded by a vision transformer based on the Perception Encoder and projected into the language model embeddings, one embedding per 40x40 pixel patch. ","+","+The model is released with two checkpoints:","+- [`thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small`](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small)","+- [`thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8`](https://huggingface.co/thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8)","+","+Both checkpoints contain quantized layers. `Inkling-2-Small` has both NVFP4 and MXFP8 quantized decoder layers. `Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8` contains only MXFP8 quantized layers. Currently only the `Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8` checkpoint is supported.","+","+","+## Resources","+","+- [Thinking Machines Blog](https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-small/)","+- [Hugging Face Blog](https://huggingface.co/blog/thinkingmachines-inkling)","+","+","+<hfoptions id=\"usage\">","+<hfoption id=\"Pipeline\">","+","+```python","+import torch","+","+from transformers import pipeline","+","+pipe = pipeline(","+    \"image-text-to-text\", model=\"thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8\", dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"auto\"","+)","+","+messages = [","+    {","+        \"role\": \"user\",","+        \"content\": [","+            {","+                \"type\": \"image\",","+                \"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/pipeline-cat-chonk.jpeg\",","+            },","+            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"What animal is in this image, and where is it?\"},","+        ],","+    },","+]","+","+output = pipe(messages, max_new_tokens=1024, return_full_text=False, skip_special_tokens=False)","+print(output[0][\"generated_text\"])","+# <|message_model|><|content_thinking|>The user is asking to identify the animal and location in the image. Need answer based on visible content. The animal looks like a Pallas's cat (Otocolobus manul), also called manul:","+# ...","+# <|end_message|><|message_model|><|content_text|>The animal is a **Pallas’s cat** (also called a **manul**). It’s walking through **snow** in front of birch logs, likely in a **zoo or enclosed habitat**. The exact geographic location can’t be determined from the image alone; in the wild they’re native to parts of **Central Asia**.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>","+```","+","+</hfoption>","+<hfoption id=\"AutoModel\">","+","+```python","+import torch","+","+from transformers import AutoModelForMultimodalLM, AutoProcessor","+","+model_id = \"thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small-MXFP8\"","+processor = AutoProcessor.from_pretrained(model_id)","+model = AutoModelForMultimodalLM.from_pretrained(model_id, dtype=torch.bfloat16, device_map=\"auto\")","+","+messages = [","+    {","+        \"role\": \"user\",","+        \"content\": [","+            {","+                \"type\": \"image\",","+                \"image\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/huggingface/documentation-images/resolve/main/pipeline-cat-chonk.jpeg\",","+            },","+            {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"What animal is in this image, and where is it?\"},","+        ],","+    },","+]","+","+inputs = processor.apply_chat_template(","+    messages,","+    tokenize=True,","+    add_generation_prompt=True,","+    return_dict=True,","+    return_tensors=\"pt\",","+).to(model.device)","+input_len = inputs[\"input_ids\"].shape[-1]","+","+outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=1024)","+print(processor.decode(outputs[0][input_len:], skip_special_tokens=False))","+# <|message_model|><|content_thinking|>The user is asking to identify the animal and location in the image. Need answer based on visible content. The animal looks like a Pallas's cat (Otocolobus manul), also called manul:","+# ...","+# <|end_message|><|message_model|><|content_text|>The animal is a **Pallas’s cat** (also called a **manul**). It’s walking through **snow** in front of birch logs, likely in a **zoo or enclosed habitat**. The exact geographic location can’t be determined from the image alone; in the wild they’re native to parts of **Central Asia**.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>","+```","+","+</hfoption>","+</hfoptions>","+","+## Notes","+","+- Attention runs in eager mode only, because every layer adds a relative position bias and a sink.","+","+## Inkling2Config","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2Config","+","+## Inkling2TextConfig","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2TextConfig","+","+## Inkling2VisionConfig","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2VisionConfig","+","+## Inkling2PreTrainedModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2PreTrainedModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2TextModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2TextModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2ForCausalLM","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2ForCausalLM","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2VisionModel","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2VisionModel","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2Model","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2Model","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2ForConditionalGeneration","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2ForConditionalGeneration","+    - forward","+","+## Inkling2ImageProcessor","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2ImageProcessor","+","+## Inkling2Processor","+","+[[autodoc]] Inkling2Processor"],"additions":166,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/conversion_mapping.py","lines":["@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@","     Concatenate,","     ErnieFuseAndSplitTextVisionExperts,","     GroupWeightRename,","+    Inkling2IndexOffsetWeightRename,","     Interleave,","     MergeModulelist,","     PermuteForRope,","@@ -258,6 +259,100 @@ def _build_checkpoint_conversion_mapping():","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp_norm\", target_patterns=r\"post_attention_layernorm\"),","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn_norm\", target_patterns=r\"input_layernorm\"),","         ],","+        \"inkling2\": [","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.unembed\\.weight\", target_patterns=r\"lm_head.weight\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.language_model.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.backbone\\.embeddings\\.\",","+                target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.embeddings.\",","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"vision_tower\\.embeddings\\.position_embedding\",","+                target_patterns=r\"vision_tower.embeddings.position_embedding.weight\",","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.backbone\\.ln_pre\\.\",","+                target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.pre_layernorm.\",","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.backbone\\.layers\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.layers.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.proj_in\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.merger.linear_1.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"model\\.visual\\.proj_out\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.vision_tower.merger.linear_2.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.ln_1\\.\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.layernorm_before.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.ln_2\\.\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.layernorm_after.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.mlp\\.c_fc\\.\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.mlp.fc1.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.mlp\\.c_proj\\.\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.mlp.fc2.\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.ls_1\\.gamma\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.lambda_1\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(vision_tower\\.layers\\.\\d+)\\.ls_2\\.gamma\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.lambda_2\"","+            ),","+        ],","+        \"inkling2_text\": [","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.unembed\\.weight\", target_patterns=r\"lm_head.weight\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"model\\.llm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"model.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"embed\\.weight\", target_patterns=r\"embed_tokens.weight\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"embed_norm\\.\", target_patterns=r\"embed_tokens.embed_norm.\"),","+            WeightConverter(","+                source_patterns=r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight\",","+                target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.gate_up_proj\",","+                operations=[Interleave(dim=1)],","+            ),","+            WeightConverter(","+                source_patterns=r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w13_weight_scale\",","+                target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.gate_up_proj_scale_inv\",","+                operations=[Interleave(dim=1)],","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight\", target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.down_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"mlp\\.experts\\.w2_weight_scale\", target_patterns=r\"mlp.experts.down_proj_scale_inv\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp.gate.bias\", target_patterns=r\"mlp.gate.e_score_correction_bias\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.wq_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.q_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.wk_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.k_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.wv_dv\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.v_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.wr_du\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.r_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.wo_ud\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.o_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.gate_attn\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.gate_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn\\.attn_sink_proj\", target_patterns=r\"self_attn.sink_proj\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"\\.attn\\.(q_l2_clip|k_l2_clip|rel_l2_clip|k_sconv|v_sconv|rel_logits_proj)\\.\",","+                target_patterns=r\".self_attn.\\1.\",","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"post_attention_convolution.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp_sconv\\.\", target_patterns=r\"post_mlp_convolution.\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"(convolution|sconv)\\.weight(?!_)\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.conv1d.weight\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"(convolution|sconv)\\.static_w\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.static_weight\"),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"(convolution|sconv)\\.weight_proj\", target_patterns=r\"\\1.weight_proj.weight\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"mlp_norm\", target_patterns=r\"post_attention_layernorm\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn_norm\", target_patterns=r\"input_layernorm\"),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"(q|k|v)_input_norm\", target_patterns=r\"\\1_input_layernorm\"),","+            Inkling2IndexOffsetWeightRename(","+                source_patterns=r\"attn_res\\.attn_queries\\.(\\d+)\",","+                target_patterns=r\"layers.\\1.attention_input.query\",","+                offset=1,","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(","+                source_patterns=r\"attn_res\\.mlp_queries\\.(\\d+)\", target_patterns=r\"layers.\\1.mlp_input.query\"","+            ),","+            WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"attn_res\\.output_query\", target_patterns=r\"final_input.query\"),","+        ],","         \"GPTNeoXForCausalLM\": [","             WeightRenaming(source_patterns=r\"^embed_out\\.\", target_patterns=\"lm_head.\"),","         ],"],"additions":95,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/core_model_loading.py","lines":["@@ -1150,6 +1150,37 @@ def reverse_transform(self) -> GroupWeightRename:","         return result"," "," ","+class Inkling2IndexOffsetWeightRename(WeightRenaming):","+    \"\"\"","+    Special case of WeightRenaming that also shifts the captured index by `offset`. Use this when a checkpoint stores","+    per-layer weights in a list that does not start at layer 0, e.g. `attn_queries.{i}` belonging to `layers.{i + 1}`.","+    \"\"\"","+","+    __slots__ = (\"offset\",)","+","+    def __init__(self, source_patterns: str | list[str], target_patterns: str | list[str], offset: int):","+        self.offset = offset","+        super().__init__(source_patterns=source_patterns, target_patterns=target_patterns)","+","+    def rename_source_key(self, source_key: str) -> tuple[str, str | None]:","+        matched = self._scoped_match(source_key)","+        if matched is None:","+            return source_key, None","+","+        prefix_dot, key_to_match, match_object = matched","+        self._was_used = True","+        matching_group_name = next(name for name, val in match_object.groupdict().items() if val is not None)","+        index = int(match_object.group(self.compiled_sources.groupindex[matching_group_name] + 1))","+        replacement = self.target_patterns[0].replace(r\"\\1\", str(index + self.offset))","+        renamed_key = key_to_match.replace(match_object.group(0), replacement, 1)","+        if prefix_dot is not None:","+            renamed_key = prefix_dot + renamed_key","+        return renamed_key, self.source_patterns[int(matching_group_name[1:])]","+","+    def reverse_transform(self) -> Inkling2IndexOffsetWeightRename:","+        return self.copy(self._original_target_patterns, self._original_source_patterns, offset=-self.offset)","+","+"," class PrefixChange(WeightRenaming):","     \"\"\"","     Special case of WeightRenaming, used to simplify adding/removing full parts of a weight name. The regexes"],"additions":31,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/exporters/exporter_dynamo.py","lines":["@@ -440,6 +440,7 @@ def _to_batched(t):","     \"transformers.models.video_llama_3.modeling_video_llama_3.VideoLlama3VisionAttention.forward\",","     \"transformers.models.paddleocr_vl.modeling_paddleocr_vl.PaddleOCRVisionAttention.forward\",","     \"transformers.models.minimax_m3_vl.modeling_minimax_m3_vl.MiniMaxM3VLVisionAttention.forward\",","+    \"transformers.models.inkling2.modeling_inkling2.Inkling2VisionAttention.forward\",","     # NaViT (1, T, D) + separate `_proj` + `.out_proj` (tuple return)","     \"transformers.models.minicpm_ocr.modeling_minicpm_ocr.MiniCPMOcrVisionAttention.forward\",","     \"transformers.models.minicpmv4_6.modeling_minicpmv4_6.MiniCPMV4_6VisionAttention.forward\","],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformers/integrations/finegrained_fp8.py","lines":["@@ -742,6 +742,8 @@ def __init__(","         self.swiglu_limit = getattr(config, \"swiglu_limit\", None)","         self.act_fn = ACT2FN[_first_attr(config, \"hidden_activation\", \"hidden_act\")]","         self.limit = getattr(config, \"swiglu_limit\", None)","+        self.gate_softcap = getattr(config, \"mlp_gate_softcap\", None)","+        self.up_softcap = getattr(config, \"mlp_up_softcap\", None)"," ","         # Expert weight precision is FP8 by default; DeepSeek V4-style models declare","         # `expert_dtype = \"fp4\"` for FP4-packed expert weights. FP4 storage:","@@ -787,6 +789,13 @@ def __init__("," ","     def _apply_gate(self, gate_up: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:","         gate, up = gate_up.chunk(2, dim=-1)","+        if self.gate_softcap is not None:","+            # Softcapped SwiGLU (e.g. Inkling2, same math as the model's non-quantized experts)","+            input_dtype = gate.dtype","+            gate, up = gate.float(), up.float()","+            gate_factor = torch.tanh(gate / self.gate_softcap) * self.gate_softcap","+            up = torch.tanh(up / self.up_softcap) * self.up_softcap","+            return (gate_factor * torch.sigmoid(gate) * up).to(input_dtype)","         if self.swiglu_alpha is not None:","             # Clamped SwiGLU-OAI gate (same math as the model's non-quantized experts).","             gate = gate.clamp(max=self.swiglu_limit)"],"additions":9,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/transformer